  "feesApplyText": "Tenants' Guide to Charges\n\nJOHNS&CO is a member of and covered by the ARLA / Propertymark Client Money Protection Scheme, and a member of a redress scheme provided by The Property Ombudsman. The charges that apply to you depend on the type of tenancy you enter into.\n\nPart One\n\nAssured Periodic Tenancy\n\nUnder the terms of the Tenant Fee Act, if you enter into an assured periodic tenancy, the following payments may apply.\n\nTenancy Deposit\n\n5 or 6 weeks' rent depending upon the rental amount, or a Deposit Replacement Insurance Product at a cost equal to 1 week's rent where offered by the Landlord.\n\nHolding Deposit\n\nEquivalent of one week's rent, which will be put towards your first rent due on completion of the tenancy.\n\nEarly Termination (requested by the tenant)\n\nA charge not exceeding the financial loss experienced by the landlord.\n\nLate Payment of Rent\n\nLimited to interest charged at 3% above the Bank of England base rate, when rent is more than 14 days late.\n\nLost Key or Security Device\n\nEquivalent to the cost incurred.\n\nChanging Tenancy Documents (after commencement)\n\n\u00a341.67 (\u00a350 inc. VAT), or any reasonable costs incurred if these are higher.\n\nStamp Duty Land Tax\n\nPayable on tenancies where the rent, for the whole time a tenant stays in the property, exceeds \u00a3125,000.\n\nHousehold Outgoings\n\nUtilities, communication services, TV licence and council tax.\n\nPart Two\n\nNon-Housing Act Tenancy\n\nWhich tenancy applies to you?\n\nA Non-Housing Act Tenancy is formed when one of the following criteria is in place:\n\nThe annual rent exceeds \u00a3100,000\nThe property is not used as a main or primary home\nThe property is occupied by an entity (company let) rather than an individual\nThere is a Resident Landlord\nPlease speak with our branch staff if you need clarity on which tenancy might apply in your circumstances.\n\nUnder the terms of the Tenant Fee Act, if you enter into a Non-Housing Act Tenancy, the following payments may apply.\n\nTenancy Setup Fee\n\nDrafting and execution of the tenancy agreement if supplied by us; collecting and holding the Tenancy Deposit as Stakeholder; issuing relevant deposit protection certificates (where applicable).\n\u00a3300 Excl. VAT\n\u00a3360 Incl. VAT\n\nCheck-in Fee\n\nChecking into the property and reviewing the inventory.\nfrom \u00a3115 Excl. VAT\nfrom \u00a3138 Incl. VAT\n\nComprehensive Reference Fee\n\nPer person, per company, and per guarantor (if required).\n\u00a350 Excl. VAT\n\u00a360 Incl. VAT\n\nRenewal Administration\n\nNegotiating and drafting an extension to the fixed term.\n\u00a3150 Excl. VAT\n\u00a3180 Incl. VAT\n\nChange of Sharer\n\nDuring a fixed term.\n\u00a3625 Excl. VAT\n\u00a3750 Incl. VAT\n\nChange of Sharer\n\nAt renewal of a fixed term.\n\u00a3250 Excl. VAT\n\u00a3300 Incl. VAT\n\nEarly Termination\n\nDeed of Surrender.\n\u00a3125 Excl. VAT\n\u00a3150 Incl. VAT\n\nLate Payment of Rent\n\nInterest charged at 3% above the Bank of England base rate\n\nHow to Pay\n\nThe holding deposit can be paid on the Goodlord platform by debit card only. All other monies due must be paid via the Goodlord platform or into JOHNS&CO's client account by direct bank transfer.\n\nWe are unable to accept cash. We do not accept credit cards.\n",
